# Windows launchers must keep CRLF endings.
#
# Without this, git checks .bat files out with LF on a fresh clone (or after a
# core.autocrlf change), and cmd.exe can mis-parse the `rem` header block and
# swallow the command that follows it. The CRLF normalisation in
# 启动GUI.bat is therefore not durable unless it is pinned here.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# Python and Markdown track the repo's actual line endings (CRLF on this
# Windows desktop tool). Pinning eol=lf here while the working tree is CRLF
# makes git warn on every commit ("CRLF will be replaced by LF"), so we match
# reality instead. A future mass renormalise to LF would let this switch back.
*.py text eol=crlf
*.md text eol=crlf
